### Day 10 - API Versioning Test Evidence

### 1. Login user -> expect 200 with token
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser09@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. v1 ticket endpoint without token -> expect 401
GET http://localhost:8081/api/v1/tickets

### 3. v1 ticket endpoint with USER token -> expect 200
# Replace TOKEN with the token from request 1
GET http://localhost:8081/api/v1/tickets
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

### 4. v1 get single ticket by id with USER token -> expect 200
# Replace TOKEN with the token from request 1
# Replace the id below with an actual id returned by request 3
GET http://localhost:8081/api/v1/tickets/REPLACE_WITH_REAL_ID
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

### 5. v1 create ticket with USER token -> expect 201
# Replace TOKEN with the token from request 1
POST http://localhost:8081/api/v1/tickets
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Monitor flickering",
  "description": "Second monitor flickers on startup.",
  "category": "Hardware",
  "priority": "LOW",
  "createdBy": "testuser09@example.com"
}

### 6. Old /api/tickets endpoint still works with USER token -> expect 200
# Replace TOKEN with the token from request 1
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

